---
title: "daily_logout_batch (kintai-v3: Initial Schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_trigger: batch logout operation triggered (server-side or admin)
    q_trigger --> q_execute: process mass logout for all active users
    q_execute --> q_count: count affected users
    q_count --> q_log_success: operation completed without error
    q_count --> q_log_error: operation encountered error

    q_log_success --> q_insert: INSERT daily_logout_logs (status = 'success', affected_count = N)
    q_log_error --> q_insert: INSERT daily_logout_logs (status = 'error', affected_count = N)

    q_insert --> q_set_defaults: executed_at = now(), id = gen_random_uuid()
    q_set_defaults --> [*]: log record created

    note right of q_trigger
        INV-001: Only admins can access daily_logout_logs (RLS policy)
        INV-002: status must be exactly 'success' or 'error' (CHECK constraint)
    end note

    note right of q_count
        INV-003: affected_count is NOT NULL - must always record how many users were affected
        INV-004: executed_at defaults to now() for automatic timestamping
    end note
